Subject: [PATCH] serial: qcom-geni: keep serving the interrupt while the port suspends

uart_suspend_port() sets uport->suspended first.  Only after that does it
stop the transmitter and the receiver under the port lock, and the port's
interrupt stays enabled until qcom_geni_serial_shutdown() disables it.
The handler returns IRQ_NONE as soon as the port is marked suspended,
without reading or clearing the engine's interrupt status.  The line is
level-triggered, so any status latched in that window keeps it asserted:
received data, or the cancels issued by stop_rx() and stop_tx().  When
the interrupt targets the CPU that runs the suspend, the CPU takes it
again as soon as the locked section ends, and the suspend makes no
further progress.  After 100,000 unhandled interrupts the
spurious-interrupt detector disables the line:

  irq 191: nobody cared (try booting with the "irqpoll" option)
  ...
   _raw_spin_unlock_irq+0x1c/0x60 (P)
   qcom_geni_serial_suspend+0x60/0x78
   dpm_run_callback+0x8c/0x19c
  ...
  Disabling IRQ #191

With its interrupt gone the port receives nothing after resume.  On a
Bluetooth UART, every HCI command then times out.

The window opened when system suspend moved out of the noirq phase.
Clearing the status and returning IRQ_HANDLED while suspended would end
the storm, but it would drop a TX DMA completion.  start_tx_dma() does
nothing while tx_dma_addr is still set, so transmission would stall
after resume.  Instead, serve the interrupt as before the port was
marked suspended.  The handler cannot run on an unclocked engine:
shutdown() disables the interrupt and waits for a running handler before
uart_change_pm() turns the resources off, and startup() enables it again
only after they are back on.

Fixes: b1f84dd32166 ("tty: serial: qcom_geni_serial: Rectify UART suspend mechanism")

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -1067,9 +1067,11 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_geni_serial_isr(
 	struct tty_port *tport = &uport->state->port;
 	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = to_dev_port(uport);
 
-	if (uport->suspended)
-		return IRQ_NONE;
-
+	/*
+	 * Serve the interrupt even once uart_suspend_port() has marked the
+	 * port suspended: RX and TX are stopped after that, and shutdown()
+	 * masks the level-triggered interrupt only then.
+	 */
 	uart_port_lock(uport);
 
 	m_irq_status = readl(uport->membase + SE_GENI_M_IRQ_STATUS);
